     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. Some references allow 2,000 to 3,000 mg/day. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day. This order is about twice the maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. They add no glycemic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a reason for the order note. I'll enter it as you direct. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
